INSERT INTO `chat_messages` VALUES (29,10,'user','Is narra safe to keep around my cat?',NULL,NULL,'complete','2026-10-22 00:25:46','2026-10-22 00:25:46',NULL,'friendly'),(30,10,'assistant','Some ornamental plants are irritating or toxic to pets, so check the species before assuming it is safe. If your cat chews the leaves and drools, vomits or seems unwell, contact a veterinarian. Placing the plant out of reach is the simplest precaution.',NULL,NULL,'complete','2026-10-22 00:25:50','2026-10-22 00:25:50',NULL,'friendly'),(31,11,'user','How much sunlight does a pandan need?',NULL,NULL,'complete','2026-09-26 11:14:00','2026-09-26 11:14:00',NULL,'formal'),(32,11,'assistant','A pandan generally grows best with the light it gets in its natural habitat. Start with bright, indirect light and watch the leaves: pale or stretched growth means it wants more light, while scorched brown patches mean it is getting too much direct sun.',NULL,NULL,'complete','2026-09-26 11:14:04','2026-09-26 11:14:04',NULL,'friendly'),(33,12,'user','Is dama de noche safe to keep around my cat?',NULL,NULL,'complete','2026-07-26 10:44:50','2026-07-26 10:44:50',NULL,'friendly'),(34,12,'assistant','Some ornamental plants are irritating or toxic to pets, so check the species before assuming it is safe. If your cat chews the leaves and drools, vomits or seems unwell, contact a veterinarian. Placing the plant out of reach is the simplest precaution.',NULL,NULL,'complete','2026-07-26 10:44:54','2026-07-26 10:44:54',NULL,'friendly'),(35,13,'user','Why are the tips of my tanglad leaves turning brown?',NULL,NULL,'complete','2026-10-20 00:21:39','2026-10-20 00:21:39',NULL,'scientific'),(36,13,'assistant','Brown tips usually point to watering stress or dry air. Check that the pot drains well, water thoroughly only when the top of the soil is dry, and avoid placing it near fans or air conditioning. Trim the brown tips with clean scissors if you like; they will not turn green again.',NULL,NULL,'complete','2026-10-20 00:21:43','2026-10-20 00:21:43',NULL,'friendly'),(37,14,'user','Is ylang-ylang safe to keep around my cat?',NULL,NULL,'complete','2026-10-21 01:47:21','2026-10-21 01:47:21',NULL,'formal'),(38,14,'assistant','Some ornamental plants are irritating or toxic to pets, so check the species before assuming it is safe. If your cat chews the leaves and drools, vomits or seems unwell, contact a veterinarian. Placing the plant out of reach is the simplest precaution.',NULL,NULL,'complete','2026-10-21 01:47:25','2026-10-21 01:47:25',NULL,'friendly'),(39,15,'user','Why are the tips of my snake plant leaves turning brown?',NULL,NULL,'complete','2026-10-14 06:04:21','2026-10-14 06:04:21',NULL,'friendly'),(40,15,'assistant','Brown tips usually point to watering stress or dry air. Check that the pot drains well, water thoroughly only when the top of the soil is dry, and avoid placing it near fans or air conditioning. Trim the brown tips with clean scissors if you like; they will not turn green again.',NULL,NULL,'complete','2026-10-14 06:04:25','2026-10-14 06:04:25',NULL,'friendly'),(41,16,'user','How do I propagate a banaba?',NULL,NULL,'complete','2026-10-22 07:41:24','2026-10-22 07:41:24',NULL,'simple'),(42,16,'assistant','Many plants like banaba can be propagated from stem cuttings. Cut just below a node with clean shears, remove the lower leaves and root it in water or moist soil in bright, indirect light. Roots usually appear in two to six weeks depending on the plant and the temperature.',NULL,NULL,'complete','2026-10-22 07:41:28','2026-10-22 07:41:28',NULL,'friendly'),(43,17,'user','How do I propagate a anthurium?',NULL,NULL,'complete','2026-08-16 07:42:04','2026-08-16 07:42:04',NULL,'friendly'),(44,17,'assistant','Many plants like anthurium can be propagated from stem cuttings. Cut just below a node with clean shears, remove the lower leaves and root it in water or moist soil in bright, indirect light. Roots usually appear in two to six weeks depending on the plant and the temperature.',NULL,NULL,'complete','2026-08-16 07:42:08','2026-08-16 07:42:08',NULL,'friendly'),(45,18,'user','Is gumamela safe to keep around my cat?',NULL,NULL,'complete','2026-08-21 23:30:41','2026-08-21 23:30:41',NULL,'friendly'),(46,18,'assistant','Some ornamental plants are irritating or toxic to pets, so check the species before assuming it is safe. If your cat chews the leaves and drools, vomits or seems unwell, contact a veterinarian. Placing the plant out of reach is the simplest precaution.',NULL,NULL,'complete','2026-08-21 23:30:45','2026-08-21 23:30:45',NULL,'friendly'),(47,19,'user','Is fiddle-leaf fig safe to keep around my cat?',NULL,NULL,'complete','2026-10-05 16:32:21','2026-10-05 16:32:21',NULL,'friendly'),(48,19,'assistant','Some ornamental plants are irritating or toxic to pets, so check the species before assuming it is safe. If your cat chews the leaves and drools, vomits or seems unwell, contact a veterinarian. Placing the plant out of reach is the simplest precaution.',NULL,NULL,'complete','2026-10-05 16:32:25','2026-10-05 16:32:25',NULL,'friendly'),(49,20,'user','How much sunlight does a waling-waling need?',NULL,NULL,'complete','2026-10-14 05:11:07','2026-10-14 05:11:07',NULL,'simple'),(50,20,'assistant','A waling-waling generally grows best with the light it gets in its natural habitat. Start with bright, indirect light and watch the leaves: pale or stretched growth means it wants more light, while scorched brown patches mean it is getting too much direct sun.',NULL,NULL,'complete','2026-10-14 05:11:11','2026-10-14 05:11:11',NULL,'friendly'),(51,21,'user','How much sunlight does a zz plant need?',NULL,NULL,'complete','2026-10-16 14:38:39','2026-10-16 14:38:39',NULL,'scientific'),(52,21,'assistant','A zz plant generally grows best with the light it gets in its natural habitat. Start with bright, indirect light and watch the leaves: pale or stretched growth means it wants more light, while scorched brown patches mean it is getting too much